window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b139-f868287dca7ceb08.json"]={sha256:"f868287dca7ceb080be3f87d1878462507d33161167fc4fb69c4e358db73444e",value:{"id":"b139","title":"潛盾機刀具磨耗管理","titleEn":"TBM cutter-wear management","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦以刀具軌跡、接觸荷重與磨耗證據解釋掘進刀具壽命。沿著調查依據、物理作用、數量估算、現場驗證到工程交接逐項建立可追溯的推論鏈，特別辨別單一數值無法揭露的空間差異及時間效應。以獨立量測檢驗簡化模型，並把觀測結果、教學假設與需要主管工程師審查的決策清楚分列。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on explain cutter life using trajectories, contact loads and wear evidence. It develops a traceable reasoning chain from evidence and physical processes through quantitative estimates, field verification and engineering handover. Spatial variation and time effects are separated from a single nominal result. Independent observations test the simplified models, while measured evidence, teaching assumptions and decisions requiring the responsible engineer remain explicitly distinguished.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-tbm","subcategoryTitle":"潛盾與掘進系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Shield and tunnel-boring systems","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-tbm","learningTags":["underground","ug-tbm","tbm"],"architectureFamily":"tbm","architectureNodes":[["刀具半徑與行程","Cutter radius and travel"],["推力分配與偏載","Thrust distribution and uneven loading"],["磨耗率與地層分段","Wear rate by geological reach"],["衝擊與混合面循環","Impact and mixed-face cycling"],["維護決策與檢查界線","Maintenance decisions and access boundaries"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[3,1]],"diagram":{"type":"tbm","labels":["刀具半徑與行程","推力分配與偏載","磨耗率與地層分段","衝擊與混合面循環","維護決策與檢查界線"],"labelsEn":["Cutter radius and travel","Thrust distribution and uneven loading","Wear rate by geological reach","Impact and mixed-face cycling","Maintenance decisions and access boundaries"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學算例，所有輸入是為比較機制而假設，並非任何地標的實測資料。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設刀位半徑5 m、轉速4 rpm，切向速度v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s；不代表建議轉速。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設推進30 mm/min、轉速3 rpm，每轉進尺p=10 mm/rev；未提供刀具容許荷重。將第一式的一個線性乘數加倍而固定其他邊界，該項貢獻隨之加倍；若為非線性式則必須重新代入，不能等比例外推。把輸入值、單位換算、計算結果及假設列成四欄，再用獨立計算器重算；最後比較量測誤差與模型簡化，判斷改變是否足以支持工程決策。","textEn":"Original teaching example: all inputs are assumptions for comparing mechanisms, not measurements from a landmark project. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume cutter radius 5 m and rotation 4 rpm; tangential speed v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s, not a recommended speed. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume advance 30 mm/min and rotation 3 rpm; penetration p=10 mm/rev, without specifying allowable cutter load. Doubling one linear multiplicative input in the first relation while holding the remaining boundaries fixed doubles that contribution; a nonlinear relation must instead be evaluated again. Tabulate inputs, unit conversions, results and assumptions in separate columns, and recalculate independently. Finally compare measurement uncertainty with model simplification before deciding whether the difference supports an engineering decision.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b139-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「刀具半徑與行程」與「貫入與每轉進尺」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cutter radius and travel\" and \"Penetration per revolution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b139-v14-01","title":"刀具半徑與行程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cutter radius and travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「刀具半徑與行程」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cutter radius and travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"不同半徑刀具每轉走過不同距離，外緣刀即使承受相同轉數也有較長接觸路徑。磨耗比較須規一化里程或體積並保留刀位，不能用更換次數直接推斷材料品質。 假設刀位半徑5 m、轉速4 rpm，切向速度v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s；不代表建議轉速。 把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「刀具半徑與行程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tools at different radii travel different distances per revolution. Outer cutters therefore accumulate longer contact paths at equal revolutions, requiring wear normalization by travel or excavation and retention of cutter position rather than replacement count alone. Assume cutter radius 5 m and rotation 4 rpm; tangential speed v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s, not a recommended speed. Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends. The resulting life model loses comparability for the next geological reach. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cutter radius and travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「刀具半徑與行程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cutter radius and travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-01-k1","title":"刀具半徑與行程","titleEn":"Cutter radius and travel","text":"不同半徑刀具每轉走過不同距離，外緣刀即使承受相同轉數也有較長接觸路徑。磨耗比較須規一化里程或體積並保留刀位，不能用更換次數直接推斷材料品質。","textEn":"Tools at different radii travel different distances per revolution. Outer cutters therefore accumulate longer contact paths at equal revolutions, requiring wear normalization by travel or excavation and retention of cutter position rather than replacement count alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「刀具半徑與行程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cutter radius and travel\" is correct?","options":["所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。","不同半徑刀具每轉走過不同距離，外緣刀即使承受相同轉數也有較長接觸路徑。","每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。"],"optionsEn":["Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position.","Tools at different radii travel different distances per revolution.","Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同半徑刀具每轉走過不同距離，外緣刀即使承受相同轉數也有較長接觸路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tools at different radii travel different distances per revolution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b139-v14-02","title":"刀具半徑與行程：定量估算","titleEn":"Cutter radius and travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「刀具半徑與行程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cutter radius and travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設刀位半徑5 m、轉速4 rpm，切向速度v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s；不代表建議轉速。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume cutter radius 5 m and rotation 4 rpm; tangential speed v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s, not a recommended speed. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以刀位圖、轉數及地層日誌計算接觸行程，對照同類刀具的量測磨耗；將外緣與中心刀分組比較，無法追溯位置的磨耗資料不得直接用於壽命排名。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Combine cutter map, revolutions and geology to calculate travel and compare measured wear for like tools; group outer and center positions separately and do not rank life from records lacking position traceability.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設刀位半徑5 m、轉速4 rpm，切向速度v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s；不代表建議轉速。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume cutter radius 5 m and rotation 4 rpm; tangential speed v=2πrn/60=2.094 m/s, not a recommended speed.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「刀具半徑與行程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cutter radius and travel\", which statement holds?","options":["旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。","刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal.","Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b139-v14-03","title":"刀具半徑與行程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cutter radius and travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「刀具半徑與行程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cutter radius and travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以刀位圖、轉數及地層日誌計算接觸行程，對照同類刀具的量測磨耗；將外緣與中心刀分組比較，無法追溯位置的磨耗資料不得直接用於壽命排名。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Combine cutter map, revolutions and geology to calculate travel and compare measured wear for like tools; group outer and center positions separately and do not rank life from records lacking position traceability. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends. The resulting life model loses comparability for the next geological reach. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄刀具半徑與行程的資料來源與適用條件。以刀位圖、轉數及地層日誌計算接觸行程，對照同類刀具的量測磨耗；將外緣與中心刀分組比較，無法追溯位置的磨耗資料不得直接用於壽命排名。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for cutter radius and travel. Combine cutter map, revolutions and geology to calculate travel and compare measured wear for like tools; group outer and center positions separately and do not rank life from records lacking position traceability.","failure":"注意干擾：把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以刀位圖、轉數及地層日誌計算接觸行程，對照同類刀具的量測磨耗；將外緣與中心刀分組比較，無法追溯位置的磨耗資料不得直接用於壽命排名。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。","textEn":"Combine cutter map, revolutions and geology to calculate travel and compare measured wear for like tools; group outer and center positions separately and do not rank life from records lacking position traceability. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends. The resulting life model loses comparability for the next geological reach.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄刀具半徑與行程的資料來源與適用條件。以刀位圖、轉數及地層日誌計算接觸行程，對照同類刀具的量測磨耗；將外緣與中心刀分組比較，無法追溯位置的磨耗資料不得直接用於壽命排名。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for cutter radius and travel. Combine cutter map, revolutions and geology to calculate travel and compare measured wear for like tools; group outer and center positions separately and do not rank life from records lacking position traceability.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「刀具半徑與行程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cutter radius and travel\"?","options":["以刀位圖、轉數及地層日誌計算接觸行程，對照同類刀具的量測磨耗；將外緣與中心刀分組比較，無法追溯位置的磨耗資料不得直接用於壽命排名。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。"],"optionsEn":["Combine cutter map, revolutions and geology to calculate travel and compare measured wear for like tools.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以刀位圖、轉數及地層日誌計算接觸行程，對照同類刀具的量測磨耗；將外緣與中心刀分組比較，無法追溯位置的磨耗資料不得直接用於壽命排名。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Combine cutter map, revolutions and geology to calculate travel and compare measured wear for like tools; group outer and center positions separately and do not rank life from records lacking position traceability. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b139-v14-04","title":"刀具半徑與行程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cutter radius and travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「刀具半徑與行程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cutter radius and travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends. The resulting life model loses comparability for the next geological reach. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resulting life model loses comparability for the next geological reach.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。","textEn":"Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends. The resulting life model loses comparability for the next geological reach.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「刀具半徑與行程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cutter radius and travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。","每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends.","Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把外緣刀較快磨耗全歸於材料缺陷會錯判供應品質，刀位更換後仍沿用舊行程又會污染趨勢；壽命模型因此對下一段地層失去可比性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attributing faster outer wear solely to material defects misjudges quality, while retaining old travel after relocation corrupts trends. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b139-v14-05","title":"貫入與每轉進尺：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Penetration per revolution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「貫入與每轉進尺」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Penetration per revolution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"每轉進尺把推進速率與轉速連結，反映刀具每次通過的切入尺度，但它也受岩體裂隙與刀具間距影響。高進尺未必代表高效率，過大載重可能使刀環或軸承提早失效。 假設推進30 mm/min、轉速3 rpm，每轉進尺p=10 mm/rev；未提供刀具容許荷重。 轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「貫入與每轉進尺」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Penetration per revolution links advance and rotation to cutting scale, but also depends on fractures and spacing. High penetration is not automatically efficient if excessive load damages cutter rings or bearings prematurely. Assume advance 30 mm/min and rotation 3 rpm; penetration p=10 mm/rev, without specifying allowable cutter load. Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting. Increasing load on that evidence may exceed tool capability when harder ground returns. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Penetration per revolution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「貫入與每轉進尺」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Penetration per revolution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-05-k1","title":"貫入與每轉進尺","titleEn":"Penetration per revolution","text":"每轉進尺把推進速率與轉速連結，反映刀具每次通過的切入尺度，但它也受岩體裂隙與刀具間距影響。高進尺未必代表高效率，過大載重可能使刀環或軸承提早失效。","textEn":"Penetration per revolution links advance and rotation to cutting scale, but also depends on fractures and spacing. High penetration is not automatically efficient if excessive load damages cutter rings or bearings prematurely.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「貫入與每轉進尺」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Penetration per revolution\" is correct?","options":["每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。","總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。","每轉進尺把推進速率與轉速連結，反映刀具每次通過的切入尺度，但它也受岩體裂隙與刀具間距影響。"],"optionsEn":["Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life.","Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load.","Penetration per revolution links advance and rotation to cutting scale, but also depends on fractures and spacing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每轉進尺把推進速率與轉速連結，反映刀具每次通過的切入尺度，但它也受岩體裂隙與刀具間距影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Penetration per revolution links advance and rotation to cutting scale, but also depends on fractures and spacing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b139-v14-06","title":"貫入與每轉進尺：定量估算","titleEn":"Penetration per revolution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「貫入與每轉進尺」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Penetration per revolution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設推進30 mm/min、轉速3 rpm，每轉進尺p=10 mm/rev；未提供刀具容許荷重。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume advance 30 mm/min and rotation 3 rpm; penetration p=10 mm/rev, without specifying allowable cutter load. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步推進、轉速、推力與扭矩，將相同地層與刀具狀態下的區段比較；刀具工程師需核對載重範圍與振動，不能只以提高每轉進尺作績效目標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize advance, rotation, thrust and torque and compare intervals with similar geology and tool condition; cutter engineers check loads and vibration instead of treating greater penetration per revolution as the sole performance objective.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設推進30 mm/min、轉速3 rpm，每轉進尺p=10 mm/rev；未提供刀具容許荷重。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume advance 30 mm/min and rotation 3 rpm; penetration p=10 mm/rev, without specifying allowable cutter load.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「貫入與每轉進尺」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Penetration per revolution\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。","班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally.","Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b139-v14-07","title":"貫入與每轉進尺：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Penetration per revolution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「貫入與每轉進尺」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Penetration per revolution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步推進、轉速、推力與扭矩，將相同地層與刀具狀態下的區段比較；刀具工程師需核對載重範圍與振動，不能只以提高每轉進尺作績效目標。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize advance, rotation, thrust and torque and compare intervals with similar geology and tool condition; cutter engineers check loads and vibration instead of treating greater penetration per revolution as the sole performance objective. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting. Increasing load on that evidence may exceed tool capability when harder ground returns. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄貫入與每轉進尺的資料來源與適用條件。同步推進、轉速、推力與扭矩，將相同地層與刀具狀態下的區段比較；刀具工程師需核對載重範圍與振動，不能只以提高每轉進尺作績效目標。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for penetration per revolution. Synchronize advance, rotation, thrust and torque and compare intervals with similar geology and tool condition; cutter engineers check loads and vibration instead of treating greater penetration per revolution as the sole performance objective.","failure":"注意干擾：轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步推進、轉速、推力與扭矩，將相同地層與刀具狀態下的區段比較；刀具工程師需核對載重範圍與振動，不能只以提高每轉進尺作績效目標。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。","textEn":"Synchronize advance, rotation, thrust and torque and compare intervals with similar geology and tool condition; cutter engineers check loads and vibration instead of treating greater penetration per revolution as the sole performance objective. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting. Increasing load on that evidence may exceed tool capability when harder ground returns.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄貫入與每轉進尺的資料來源與適用條件。同步推進、轉速、推力與扭矩，將相同地層與刀具狀態下的區段比較；刀具工程師需核對載重範圍與振動，不能只以提高每轉進尺作績效目標。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for penetration per revolution. Synchronize advance, rotation, thrust and torque and compare intervals with similar geology and tool condition; cutter engineers check loads and vibration instead of treating greater penetration per revolution as the sole performance objective.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「貫入與每轉進尺」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Penetration per revolution\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步推進、轉速、推力與扭矩，將相同地層與刀具狀態下的區段比較；刀具工程師需核對載重範圍與振動，不能只以提高每轉進尺作績效目標。","只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronize advance, rotation, thrust and torque and compare intervals with similar geology and tool condition.","Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步推進、轉速、推力與扭矩，將相同地層與刀具狀態下的區段比較；刀具工程師需核對載重範圍與振動，不能只以提高每轉進尺作績效目標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize advance, rotation, thrust and torque and compare intervals with similar geology and tool condition; cutter engineers check loads and vibration instead of treating greater penetration per revolution as the sole performance objective. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b139-v14-08","title":"貫入與每轉進尺：失效診斷","titleEn":"Penetration per revolution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「貫入與每轉進尺」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Penetration per revolution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting. Increasing load on that evidence may exceed tool capability when harder ground returns. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Increasing load on that evidence may exceed tool capability when harder ground returns.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。","textEn":"Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting. Increasing load on that evidence may exceed tool capability when harder ground returns.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「貫入與每轉進尺」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Penetration per revolution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。","轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load.","Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"轉速讀值或里程時間不一致會製造假高進尺，軟弱帶自然崩解也可能看似切削優秀；若據此增加荷重，進入硬岩後可能超出刀具能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronized speed and distance create false high penetration, while weak-ground disintegration can mimic excellent cutting. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b139-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「推力分配與偏載」與「切削比能與條件」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thrust distribution and uneven loading\" and \"Specific cutting energy and conditions\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b139-v14-09","title":"推力分配與偏載：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thrust distribution and uneven loading: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「推力分配與偏載」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thrust distribution and uneven loading” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"總推力包含刀具切削、盾體摩擦及其他阻力，除以刀具數只是粗略平均。混合面與刀盤變形會造成偏載，真正限制可能是單刀峰值而非平均，所以需要位置與工況證據。 假設扣除非切削阻力後有效推力10 MN分到40刀，平均250 kN/刀；不等於每刀實際受力。 少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「推力分配與偏載」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Total thrust includes cutting, shield friction and other resistance, making division by cutter count only a rough mean. Mixed ground and cutterhead deformation create uneven loads, with individual peaks potentially governing instead of the average. Assume effective cutting thrust 10 MN after removing other resistance, shared by 40 tools; the mean is 250 kN/tool, not each tool's actual load. A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust. Ignoring uneven loading leaves localized ring fracture unexplained and may worsen it through increased total thrust. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thrust distribution and uneven loading” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「推力分配與偏載」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thrust distribution and uneven loading”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-09-k1","title":"推力分配與偏載","titleEn":"Thrust distribution and uneven loading","text":"總推力包含刀具切削、盾體摩擦及其他阻力，除以刀具數只是粗略平均。混合面與刀盤變形會造成偏載，真正限制可能是單刀峰值而非平均，所以需要位置與工況證據。","textEn":"Total thrust includes cutting, shield friction and other resistance, making division by cutter count only a rough mean. Mixed ground and cutterhead deformation create uneven loads, with individual peaks potentially governing instead of the average.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「推力分配與偏載」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thrust distribution and uneven loading\" is correct?","options":["總推力包含刀具切削、盾體摩擦及其他阻力，除以刀具數只是粗略平均。","總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。","旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。"],"optionsEn":["Total thrust includes cutting, shield friction and other resistance, making division by cutter count only a rough mean.","Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load.","Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總推力包含刀具切削、盾體摩擦及其他阻力，除以刀具數只是粗略平均。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Total thrust includes cutting, shield friction and other resistance, making division by cutter count only a rough mean. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b139-v14-10","title":"推力分配與偏載：定量估算","titleEn":"Thrust distribution and uneven loading: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「推力分配與偏載」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thrust distribution and uneven loading” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設扣除非切削阻力後有效推力10 MN分到40刀，平均250 kN/刀；不等於每刀實際受力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume effective cutting thrust 10 MN after removing other resistance, shared by 40 tools; the mean is 250 kN/tool, not each tool's actual load. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對總推力與摩擦估算，結合刀位、混合面和可用單刀量測檢查偏載；分析報告列明平均值用途和未量測峰值，不把均分模型當作所有刀具符合能力的證明。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check thrust and friction estimates against cutter positions, mixed-face geometry and available individual measurements; state the mean's limited use and unresolved peaks instead of treating equal sharing as proof of adequate capacity everywhere.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設扣除非切削阻力後有效推力10 MN分到40刀，平均250 kN/刀；不等於每刀實際受力。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume effective cutting thrust 10 MN after removing other resistance, shared by 40 tools; the mean is 250 kN/tool, not each tool's actual load.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「推力分配與偏載」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thrust distribution and uneven loading\", which statement holds?","options":["刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b139-v14-11","title":"推力分配與偏載：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thrust distribution and uneven loading: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「推力分配與偏載」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thrust distribution and uneven loading” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對總推力與摩擦估算，結合刀位、混合面和可用單刀量測檢查偏載；分析報告列明平均值用途和未量測峰值，不把均分模型當作所有刀具符合能力的證明。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check thrust and friction estimates against cutter positions, mixed-face geometry and available individual measurements; state the mean's limited use and unresolved peaks instead of treating equal sharing as proof of adequate capacity everywhere. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust. Ignoring uneven loading leaves localized ring fracture unexplained and may worsen it through increased total thrust. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄推力分配與偏載的資料來源與適用條件。核對總推力與摩擦估算，結合刀位、混合面和可用單刀量測檢查偏載；分析報告列明平均值用途和未量測峰值，不把均分模型當作所有刀具符合能力的證明。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for thrust distribution and uneven loading. Check thrust and friction estimates against cutter positions, mixed-face geometry and available individual measurements; state the mean's limited use and unresolved peaks instead of treating equal sharing as proof of adequate capacity everywhere.","failure":"注意干擾：少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對總推力與摩擦估算，結合刀位、混合面和可用單刀量測檢查偏載；分析報告列明平均值用途和未量測峰值，不把均分模型當作所有刀具符合能力的證明。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。","textEn":"Check thrust and friction estimates against cutter positions, mixed-face geometry and available individual measurements; state the mean's limited use and unresolved peaks instead of treating equal sharing as proof of adequate capacity everywhere. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust. Ignoring uneven loading leaves localized ring fracture unexplained and may worsen it through increased total thrust.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄推力分配與偏載的資料來源與適用條件。核對總推力與摩擦估算，結合刀位、混合面和可用單刀量測檢查偏載；分析報告列明平均值用途和未量測峰值，不把均分模型當作所有刀具符合能力的證明。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for thrust distribution and uneven loading. Check thrust and friction estimates against cutter positions, mixed-face geometry and available individual measurements; state the mean's limited use and unresolved peaks instead of treating equal sharing as proof of adequate capacity everywhere.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「推力分配與偏載」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thrust distribution and uneven loading\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。","核對總推力與摩擦估算，結合刀位、混合面和可用單刀量測檢查偏載；分析報告列明平均值用途和未量測峰值，不把均分模型當作所有刀具符合能力的證明。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter.","Check thrust and friction estimates against cutter positions, mixed-face geometry and available individual measurements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對總推力與摩擦估算，結合刀位、混合面和可用單刀量測檢查偏載；分析報告列明平均值用途和未量測峰值，不把均分模型當作所有刀具符合能力的證明。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check thrust and friction estimates against cutter positions, mixed-face geometry and available individual measurements; state the mean's limited use and unresolved peaks instead of treating equal sharing as proof of adequate capacity everywhere. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b139-v14-12","title":"推力分配與偏載：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thrust distribution and uneven loading: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「推力分配與偏載」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thrust distribution and uneven loading” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust. Ignoring uneven loading leaves localized ring fracture unexplained and may worsen it through increased total thrust. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ignoring uneven loading leaves localized ring fracture unexplained and may worsen it through increased total thrust.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。","textEn":"A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust. Ignoring uneven loading leaves localized ring fracture unexplained and may worsen it through increased total thrust.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「推力分配與偏載」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thrust distribution and uneven loading\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。"],"optionsEn":["A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal."],"answer":0,"explanation":"少數刀先接觸硬塊時可能承受高衝擊而平均推力正常，若忽略偏載便無法解釋局部刀環崩裂；盲目增加總推力可能使問題惡化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A few tools meeting a hard inclusion can suffer high impact with normal mean thrust. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b139-v14-13","title":"切削比能與條件：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Specific cutting energy and conditions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「切削比能與條件」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Specific cutting energy and conditions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"扭矩功除以開挖體積得到旋轉比能，可比較破岩代價但不包含全部系統能耗。磨耗、節理及運碴再研磨都會影響它，必須將機械狀態和地質相符的區段放在一起比較。 假設平均扭矩2 MN·m、轉10圈、開挖20 m³，E=2πTn/V=6.283 MJ/m³，僅旋轉部分。 運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「切削比能與條件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rotational work per excavated volume measures cutting cost but excludes other system energy. Wear, joints and regrinding affect it, requiring matched geological and mechanical conditions for meaningful comparisons. Assume mean torque 2 MN·m, 10 revolutions and excavation 20 m³; E=2πTn/V=6.283 MJ/m³ for rotation only. Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock. Incorrect excavated volume can conversely make the energy index appear better while actual efficiency deteriorates. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Specific cutting energy and conditions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「切削比能與條件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Specific cutting energy and conditions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-13-k1","title":"切削比能與條件","titleEn":"Specific cutting energy and conditions","text":"扭矩功除以開挖體積得到旋轉比能，可比較破岩代價但不包含全部系統能耗。磨耗、節理及運碴再研磨都會影響它，必須將機械狀態和地質相符的區段放在一起比較。","textEn":"Rotational work per excavated volume measures cutting cost but excludes other system energy. Wear, joints and regrinding affect it, requiring matched geological and mechanical conditions for meaningful comparisons.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「切削比能與條件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Specific cutting energy and conditions\" is correct?","options":["旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。","扭矩功除以開挖體積得到旋轉比能，可比較破岩代價但不包含全部系統能耗。","前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。"],"optionsEn":["Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal.","Rotational work per excavated volume measures cutting cost but excludes other system energy.","The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"扭矩功除以開挖體積得到旋轉比能，可比較破岩代價但不包含全部系統能耗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rotational work per excavated volume measures cutting cost but excludes other system energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b139-v14-14","title":"切削比能與條件：定量估算","titleEn":"Specific cutting energy and conditions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「切削比能與條件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Specific cutting energy and conditions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設平均扭矩2 MN·m、轉10圈、開挖20 m³，E=2πTn/V=6.283 MJ/m³，僅旋轉部分。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume mean torque 2 MN·m, 10 revolutions and excavation 20 m³; E=2πTn/V=6.283 MJ/m³ for rotation only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將扭矩積分與實測開挖體積核對，標記停機、空轉及換刀，對照碴片尺寸與地質；比能突升先查多種成因，再由刀具與地工人員決定是否需要獨立檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check integrated torque work against measured excavation volume and mark stops, idle rotation and replacements; compare chips and geology and investigate competing causes before cutter and geotechnical specialists select further checks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設平均扭矩2 MN·m、轉10圈、開挖20 m³，E=2πTn/V=6.283 MJ/m³，僅旋轉部分。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume mean torque 2 MN·m, 10 revolutions and excavation 20 m³; E=2πTn/V=6.283 MJ/m³ for rotation only.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「切削比能與條件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Specific cutting energy and conditions\", which statement holds?","options":["班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。","只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring.","Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b139-v14-15","title":"切削比能與條件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Specific cutting energy and conditions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「切削比能與條件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Specific cutting energy and conditions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將扭矩積分與實測開挖體積核對，標記停機、空轉及換刀，對照碴片尺寸與地質；比能突升先查多種成因，再由刀具與地工人員決定是否需要獨立檢查。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check integrated torque work against measured excavation volume and mark stops, idle rotation and replacements; compare chips and geology and investigate competing causes before cutter and geotechnical specialists select further checks. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock. Incorrect excavated volume can conversely make the energy index appear better while actual efficiency deteriorates. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄切削比能與條件的資料來源與適用條件。將扭矩積分與實測開挖體積核對，標記停機、空轉及換刀，對照碴片尺寸與地質；比能突升先查多種成因，再由刀具與地工人員決定是否需要獨立檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for specific cutting energy and conditions. Check integrated torque work against measured excavation volume and mark stops, idle rotation and replacements; compare chips and geology and investigate competing causes before cutter and geotechnical specialists select further checks.","failure":"注意干擾：運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將扭矩積分與實測開挖體積核對，標記停機、空轉及換刀，對照碴片尺寸與地質；比能突升先查多種成因，再由刀具與地工人員決定是否需要獨立檢查。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。","textEn":"Check integrated torque work against measured excavation volume and mark stops, idle rotation and replacements; compare chips and geology and investigate competing causes before cutter and geotechnical specialists select further checks. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock. Incorrect excavated volume can conversely make the energy index appear better while actual efficiency deteriorates.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄切削比能與條件的資料來源與適用條件。將扭矩積分與實測開挖體積核對，標記停機、空轉及換刀，對照碴片尺寸與地質；比能突升先查多種成因，再由刀具與地工人員決定是否需要獨立檢查。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for specific cutting energy and conditions. Check integrated torque work against measured excavation volume and mark stops, idle rotation and replacements; compare chips and geology and investigate competing causes before cutter and geotechnical specialists select further checks.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「切削比能與條件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Specific cutting energy and conditions\"?","options":["將扭矩積分與實測開挖體積核對，標記停機、空轉及換刀，對照碴片尺寸與地質；比能突升先查多種成因，再由刀具與地工人員決定是否需要獨立檢查。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Check integrated torque work against measured excavation volume and mark stops, idle rotation and replacements.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將扭矩積分與實測開挖體積核對，標記停機、空轉及換刀，對照碴片尺寸與地質；比能突升先查多種成因，再由刀具與地工人員決定是否需要獨立檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check integrated torque work against measured excavation volume and mark stops, idle rotation and replacements; compare chips and geology and investigate competing causes before cutter and geotechnical specialists select further checks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b139-v14-16","title":"切削比能與條件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Specific cutting energy and conditions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「切削比能與條件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Specific cutting energy and conditions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock. Incorrect excavated volume can conversely make the energy index appear better while actual efficiency deteriorates. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Incorrect excavated volume can conversely make the energy index appear better while actual efficiency deteriorates.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。","textEn":"Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock. Incorrect excavated volume can conversely make the energy index appear better while actual efficiency deteriorates.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「切削比能與條件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Specific cutting energy and conditions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。","前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock.","The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"運碴不良造成重複碾碎會抬高比能，若誤當岩石變硬便可能錯調推力；出土體積估錯又讓能量指標看似改善而實際效率下降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Poor muck removal raises energy through regrinding and may be misread as harder rock. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b139-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「磨耗率與地層分段」與「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wear rate by geological reach\" and \"Ring wear and bearing failure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b139-v14-17","title":"磨耗率與地層分段：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wear rate by geological reach: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「磨耗率與地層分段」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wear rate by geological reach” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"刀環徑向損失反映磨蝕，但壽命並非沿全程固定線性；礦物、顆粒與含水改變會使速率跳變。計算前需把更換和刀位移動分開，且保留接近極限時的非線性劣化可能。 假設徑向磨耗3 mm歷經600 m，平均0.005 mm/m；此率不能無條件外推到下一岩層。 跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「磨耗率與地層分段」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Radial loss measures abrasion, but life is not uniformly linear along a drive. Mineralogy, grains and water change rates abruptly. Separate replacements and relocation and retain the possibility of accelerated deterioration near a limiting condition. Assume radial wear 3 mm over 600 m; mean rate is 0.005 mm/m, not transferable unconditionally to the next stratum. Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery. The resulting life estimate identifies tools requiring planned inspection too late. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wear rate by geological reach” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「磨耗率與地層分段」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wear rate by geological reach”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-17-k1","title":"磨耗率與地層分段","titleEn":"Wear rate by geological reach","text":"刀環徑向損失反映磨蝕，但壽命並非沿全程固定線性；礦物、顆粒與含水改變會使速率跳變。計算前需把更換和刀位移動分開，且保留接近極限時的非線性劣化可能。","textEn":"Radial loss measures abrasion, but life is not uniformly linear along a drive. Mineralogy, grains and water change rates abruptly.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「磨耗率與地層分段」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wear rate by geological reach\" is correct?","options":["前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。","刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。","刀環徑向損失反映磨蝕，但壽命並非沿全程固定線性；礦物、顆粒與含水改變會使速率跳變。"],"optionsEn":["The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally.","Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.","Radial loss measures abrasion, but life is not uniformly linear along a drive."],"answer":2,"explanation":"刀環徑向損失反映磨蝕，但壽命並非沿全程固定線性；礦物、顆粒與含水改變會使速率跳變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Radial loss measures abrasion, but life is not uniformly linear along a drive. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b139-v14-18","title":"磨耗率與地層分段：定量估算","titleEn":"Wear rate by geological reach: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「磨耗率與地層分段」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wear rate by geological reach” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設徑向磨耗3 mm歷經600 m，平均0.005 mm/m；此率不能無條件外推到下一岩層。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume radial wear 3 mm over 600 m; mean rate is 0.005 mm/m, not transferable unconditionally to the next stratum. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用一致量具和基準量測刀環，將磨耗對里程、轉數和岩性分段圖示；比較相似刀位與材料，壽命外推需由刀具工程師說明穩態假設，不能以全程平均掩蓋短高磨耗區。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure with consistent gauges and datum and plot wear against chainage, revolutions and geology; compare like positions and materials and require engineers to justify steady-rate extrapolation rather than hide a short severe zone in a route average.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設徑向磨耗3 mm歷經600 m，平均0.005 mm/m；此率不能無條件外推到下一岩層。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume radial wear 3 mm over 600 m; mean rate is 0.005 mm/m, not transferable unconditionally to the next stratum.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「磨耗率與地層分段」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wear rate by geological reach\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。","刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type.","Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b139-v14-19","title":"磨耗率與地層分段：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wear rate by geological reach: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「磨耗率與地層分段」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wear rate by geological reach” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用一致量具和基準量測刀環，將磨耗對里程、轉數和岩性分段圖示；比較相似刀位與材料，壽命外推需由刀具工程師說明穩態假設，不能以全程平均掩蓋短高磨耗區。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure with consistent gauges and datum and plot wear against chainage, revolutions and geology; compare like positions and materials and require engineers to justify steady-rate extrapolation rather than hide a short severe zone in a route average. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery. The resulting life estimate identifies tools requiring planned inspection too late. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄磨耗率與地層分段的資料來源與適用條件。用一致量具和基準量測刀環，將磨耗對里程、轉數和岩性分段圖示；比較相似刀位與材料，壽命外推需由刀具工程師說明穩態假設，不能以全程平均掩蓋短高磨耗區。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for wear rate by geological reach. Measure with consistent gauges and datum and plot wear against chainage, revolutions and geology; compare like positions and materials and require engineers to justify steady-rate extrapolation rather than hide a short severe zone in a route average.","failure":"注意干擾：跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用一致量具和基準量測刀環，將磨耗對里程、轉數和岩性分段圖示；比較相似刀位與材料，壽命外推需由刀具工程師說明穩態假設，不能以全程平均掩蓋短高磨耗區。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。","textEn":"Measure with consistent gauges and datum and plot wear against chainage, revolutions and geology; compare like positions and materials and require engineers to justify steady-rate extrapolation rather than hide a short severe zone in a route average. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery. The resulting life estimate identifies tools requiring planned inspection too late.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄磨耗率與地層分段的資料來源與適用條件。用一致量具和基準量測刀環，將磨耗對里程、轉數和岩性分段圖示；比較相似刀位與材料，壽命外推需由刀具工程師說明穩態假設，不能以全程平均掩蓋短高磨耗區。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for wear rate by geological reach. Measure with consistent gauges and datum and plot wear against chainage, revolutions and geology; compare like positions and materials and require engineers to justify steady-rate extrapolation rather than hide a short severe zone in a route average.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「磨耗率與地層分段」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wear rate by geological reach\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用一致量具和基準量測刀環，將磨耗對里程、轉數和岩性分段圖示；比較相似刀位與材料，壽命外推需由刀具工程師說明穩態假設，不能以全程平均掩蓋短高磨耗區。","每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure with consistent gauges and datum and plot wear against chainage, revolutions and geology.","Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用一致量具和基準量測刀環，將磨耗對里程、轉數和岩性分段圖示；比較相似刀位與材料，壽命外推需由刀具工程師說明穩態假設，不能以全程平均掩蓋短高磨耗區。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure with consistent gauges and datum and plot wear against chainage, revolutions and geology; compare like positions and materials and require engineers to justify steady-rate extrapolation rather than hide a short severe zone in a route average. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b139-v14-20","title":"磨耗率與地層分段：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wear rate by geological reach: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「磨耗率與地層分段」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wear rate by geological reach” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery. The resulting life estimate identifies tools requiring planned inspection too late. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resulting life estimate identifies tools requiring planned inspection too late.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。","textEn":"Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery. The resulting life estimate identifies tools requiring planned inspection too late.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「磨耗率與地層分段」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wear rate by geological reach\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。","跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.","Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨岩性平均會低估磨蝕帶的即時消耗，量具基準改變又會製造假回復；錯誤壽命預估可能讓需要計畫檢查的刀具過晚被辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averaging across lithologies understates current wear in an abrasive band, while changed measuring datums create false recovery. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b139-v14-21","title":"刀環磨耗與軸承故障：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring wear and bearing failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ring wear and bearing failure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"刀環磨耗是接觸表面的漸進損失，軸承故障則可能使刀具停止滾動並產生滑磨，兩者症狀不同。溫度、聲振和磨耗形態需要合併，不能只量剩餘直徑就判斷可用性。 假設正常溫度40°C、觀測65°C，升幅25 K；此差只供教學診斷，不是通用軸承警戒值。 卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ring wear is gradual surface loss, whereas bearing failure can stop rotation and create sliding abrasion. Temperature, vibration and wear shape are complementary, and remaining diameter alone cannot establish tool condition. Assume normal temperature 40°C and observation 65°C; the rise is 25 K, a diagnostic illustration rather than a universal bearing alarm. A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little. Average cutterhead signals can therefore miss the early failure of one cutter. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ring wear and bearing failure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ring wear and bearing failure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-21-k1","title":"刀環磨耗與軸承故障","titleEn":"Ring wear and bearing failure","text":"刀環磨耗是接觸表面的漸進損失，軸承故障則可能使刀具停止滾動並產生滑磨，兩者症狀不同。溫度、聲振和磨耗形態需要合併，不能只量剩餘直徑就判斷可用性。","textEn":"Ring wear is gradual surface loss, whereas bearing failure can stop rotation and create sliding abrasion. Temperature, vibration and wear shape are complementary, and remaining diameter alone cannot establish tool condition.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring wear and bearing failure\" is correct?","options":["刀環磨耗是接觸表面的漸進損失，軸承故障則可能使刀具停止滾動並產生滑磨，兩者症狀不同。","刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。","班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。"],"optionsEn":["Ring wear is gradual surface loss, whereas bearing failure can stop rotation and create sliding abrasion.","Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.","Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"刀環磨耗是接觸表面的漸進損失，軸承故障則可能使刀具停止滾動並產生滑磨，兩者症狀不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ring wear is gradual surface loss, whereas bearing failure can stop rotation and create sliding abrasion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b139-v14-22","title":"刀環磨耗與軸承故障：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring wear and bearing failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ring wear and bearing failure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設正常溫度40°C、觀測65°C，升幅25 K；此差只供教學診斷，不是通用軸承警戒值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume normal temperature 40°C and observation 65°C; the rise is 25 K, a diagnostic illustration rather than a universal bearing alarm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較同工況刀具的溫度與振動基線，檢查平磨面、偏磨及轉動狀態的核准檢查紀錄；設備主管需區分散熱環境和軸承異常，所有接近刀盤檢查遵守專業安全程序。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare temperature and vibration baselines under matched conditions with approved records of flat spots, uneven wear and rotation; equipment leads distinguish cooling changes from bearing faults, with cutterhead access restricted to specialist procedures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設正常溫度40°C、觀測65°C，升幅25 K；此差只供教學診斷，不是通用軸承警戒值。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume normal temperature 40°C and observation 65°C; the rise is 25 K, a diagnostic illustration rather than a universal bearing alarm.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring wear and bearing failure\", which statement holds?","options":["只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b139-v14-23","title":"刀環磨耗與軸承故障：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring wear and bearing failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ring wear and bearing failure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較同工況刀具的溫度與振動基線，檢查平磨面、偏磨及轉動狀態的核准檢查紀錄；設備主管需區分散熱環境和軸承異常，所有接近刀盤檢查遵守專業安全程序。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare temperature and vibration baselines under matched conditions with approved records of flat spots, uneven wear and rotation; equipment leads distinguish cooling changes from bearing faults, with cutterhead access restricted to specialist procedures. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little. Average cutterhead signals can therefore miss the early failure of one cutter. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄刀環磨耗與軸承故障的資料來源與適用條件。比較同工況刀具的溫度與振動基線，檢查平磨面、偏磨及轉動狀態的核准檢查紀錄；設備主管需區分散熱環境和軸承異常，所有接近刀盤檢查遵守專業安全程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for ring wear and bearing failure. Compare temperature and vibration baselines under matched conditions with approved records of flat spots, uneven wear and rotation; equipment leads distinguish cooling changes from bearing faults, with cutterhead access restricted to specialist procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較同工況刀具的溫度與振動基線，檢查平磨面、偏磨及轉動狀態的核准檢查紀錄；設備主管需區分散熱環境和軸承異常，所有接近刀盤檢查遵守專業安全程序。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。","textEn":"Compare temperature and vibration baselines under matched conditions with approved records of flat spots, uneven wear and rotation; equipment leads distinguish cooling changes from bearing faults, with cutterhead access restricted to specialist procedures. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little. Average cutterhead signals can therefore miss the early failure of one cutter.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄刀環磨耗與軸承故障的資料來源與適用條件。比較同工況刀具的溫度與振動基線，檢查平磨面、偏磨及轉動狀態的核准檢查紀錄；設備主管需區分散熱環境和軸承異常，所有接近刀盤檢查遵守專業安全程序。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for ring wear and bearing failure. Compare temperature and vibration baselines under matched conditions with approved records of flat spots, uneven wear and rotation; equipment leads distinguish cooling changes from bearing faults, with cutterhead access restricted to specialist procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring wear and bearing failure\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。","比較同工況刀具的溫度與振動基線，檢查平磨面、偏磨及轉動狀態的核准檢查紀錄；設備主管需區分散熱環境和軸承異常，所有接近刀盤檢查遵守專業安全程序。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load.","Compare temperature and vibration baselines under matched conditions with approved records of flat spots, uneven wear and rotation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較同工況刀具的溫度與振動基線，檢查平磨面、偏磨及轉動狀態的核准檢查紀錄；設備主管需區分散熱環境和軸承異常，所有接近刀盤檢查遵守專業安全程序。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare temperature and vibration baselines under matched conditions with approved records of flat spots, uneven wear and rotation; equipment leads distinguish cooling changes from bearing faults, with cutterhead access restricted to specialist procedures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b139-v14-24","title":"刀環磨耗與軸承故障：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring wear and bearing failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ring wear and bearing failure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little. Average cutterhead signals can therefore miss the early failure of one cutter. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Average cutterhead signals can therefore miss the early failure of one cutter.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。","textEn":"A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little. Average cutterhead signals can therefore miss the early failure of one cutter.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「刀環磨耗與軸承故障」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring wear and bearing failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。"],"optionsEn":["A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"卡死刀具會由滾動變滑動，局部發熱和刀環損失加速，總扭矩初期卻未必明顯；只靠平均刀盤訊號可能漏掉早期單刀故障。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A seized tool slides rather than rolls, accelerating heat and local wear while total torque may initially change little. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b139-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「衝擊與混合面循環」與「刀間距與碴片形成」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Impact and mixed-face cycling\" and \"Cutter spacing and chip formation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b139-v14-25","title":"衝擊與混合面循環：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Impact and mixed-face cycling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「衝擊與混合面循環」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Impact and mixed-face cycling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"刀具每轉穿越硬軟界面會反覆載入卸載，平均力無法代表疲勞與衝擊。界面位置、硬塊尺寸和旋轉速度共同控制循環數與幅值，需把事件和刀位路徑對齊。 假設每轉有2次硬軟轉換、轉速3 rpm、持續100 h，轉換次數2×3×60×100=36000次。 取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「衝擊與混合面循環」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Crossing a hard-soft interface repeatedly loads and unloads a tool. Mean force cannot represent fatigue and impact; interface position, inclusion size and rotation together control cycling, requiring events to be aligned with cutter trajectories. Assume 2 transitions per revolution at 3 rpm over 100 h; transition count is 2×3×60×100=36000. Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues. Counting revolutions without interface crossings may wrongly classify localized chipping as a random manufacturing defect rather than repeated loading. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Impact and mixed-face cycling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「衝擊與混合面循環」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Impact and mixed-face cycling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-25-k1","title":"衝擊與混合面循環","titleEn":"Impact and mixed-face cycling","text":"刀具每轉穿越硬軟界面會反覆載入卸載，平均力無法代表疲勞與衝擊。界面位置、硬塊尺寸和旋轉速度共同控制循環數與幅值，需把事件和刀位路徑對齊。","textEn":"Crossing a hard-soft interface repeatedly loads and unloads a tool. Mean force cannot represent fatigue and impact; interface position, inclusion size and rotation together control cycling, requiring events to be aligned with cutter trajectories.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「衝擊與混合面循環」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Impact and mixed-face cycling\" is correct?","options":["班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。","刀具每轉穿越硬軟界面會反覆載入卸載，平均力無法代表疲勞與衝擊。","相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。"],"optionsEn":["Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring.","Crossing a hard-soft interface repeatedly loads and unloads a tool.","The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type."],"answer":1,"explanation":"刀具每轉穿越硬軟界面會反覆載入卸載，平均力無法代表疲勞與衝擊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Crossing a hard-soft interface repeatedly loads and unloads a tool. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b139-v14-26","title":"衝擊與混合面循環：定量估算","titleEn":"Impact and mixed-face cycling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「衝擊與混合面循環」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Impact and mixed-face cycling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設每轉有2次硬軟轉換、轉速3 rpm、持續100 h，轉換次數2×3×60×100=36000次。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume 2 transitions per revolution at 3 rpm over 100 h; transition count is 2×3×60×100=36000. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：利用地質面形與旋轉訊號對照週期性衝擊，保留高頻資料而非僅班平均；刀具工程師依實際載荷幅和材料資料評估損傷，循環數本身不能換成未經驗證的剩餘壽命。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare face geometry with rotation-synchronized impacts and retain high-frequency records rather than shift means; specialists assess damage using actual amplitudes and material data, not cycle count alone as an unvalidated remaining-life prediction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設每轉有2次硬軟轉換、轉速3 rpm、持續100 h，轉換次數2×3×60×100=36000次。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume 2 transitions per revolution at 3 rpm over 100 h; transition count is 2×3×60×100=36000.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「衝擊與混合面循環」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Impact and mixed-face cycling\", which statement holds?","options":["刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。","每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter.","Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b139-v14-27","title":"衝擊與混合面循環：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Impact and mixed-face cycling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「衝擊與混合面循環」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Impact and mixed-face cycling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"利用地質面形與旋轉訊號對照週期性衝擊，保留高頻資料而非僅班平均；刀具工程師依實際載荷幅和材料資料評估損傷，循環數本身不能換成未經驗證的剩餘壽命。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare face geometry with rotation-synchronized impacts and retain high-frequency records rather than shift means; specialists assess damage using actual amplitudes and material data, not cycle count alone as an unvalidated remaining-life prediction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues. Counting revolutions without interface crossings may wrongly classify localized chipping as a random manufacturing defect rather than repeated loading. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄衝擊與混合面循環的資料來源與適用條件。利用地質面形與旋轉訊號對照週期性衝擊，保留高頻資料而非僅班平均；刀具工程師依實際載荷幅和材料資料評估損傷，循環數本身不能換成未經驗證的剩餘壽命。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for impact and mixed-face cycling. Compare face geometry with rotation-synchronized impacts and retain high-frequency records rather than shift means; specialists assess damage using actual amplitudes and material data, not cycle count alone as an unvalidated remaining-life prediction.","failure":"注意干擾：取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"利用地質面形與旋轉訊號對照週期性衝擊，保留高頻資料而非僅班平均；刀具工程師依實際載荷幅和材料資料評估損傷，循環數本身不能換成未經驗證的剩餘壽命。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。","textEn":"Compare face geometry with rotation-synchronized impacts and retain high-frequency records rather than shift means; specialists assess damage using actual amplitudes and material data, not cycle count alone as an unvalidated remaining-life prediction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues. Counting revolutions without interface crossings may wrongly classify localized chipping as a random manufacturing defect rather than repeated loading.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄衝擊與混合面循環的資料來源與適用條件。利用地質面形與旋轉訊號對照週期性衝擊，保留高頻資料而非僅班平均；刀具工程師依實際載荷幅和材料資料評估損傷，循環數本身不能換成未經驗證的剩餘壽命。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for impact and mixed-face cycling. Compare face geometry with rotation-synchronized impacts and retain high-frequency records rather than shift means; specialists assess damage using actual amplitudes and material data, not cycle count alone as an unvalidated remaining-life prediction.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「衝擊與混合面循環」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Impact and mixed-face cycling\"?","options":["利用地質面形與旋轉訊號對照週期性衝擊，保留高頻資料而非僅班平均；刀具工程師依實際載荷幅和材料資料評估損傷，循環數本身不能換成未經驗證的剩餘壽命。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。"],"optionsEn":["Compare face geometry with rotation-synchronized impacts and retain high-frequency records rather than shift means.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal."],"answer":0,"explanation":"利用地質面形與旋轉訊號對照週期性衝擊，保留高頻資料而非僅班平均；刀具工程師依實際載荷幅和材料資料評估損傷，循環數本身不能換成未經驗證的剩餘壽命。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare face geometry with rotation-synchronized impacts and retain high-frequency records rather than shift means; specialists assess damage using actual amplitudes and material data, not cycle count alone as an unvalidated remaining-life prediction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b139-v14-28","title":"衝擊與混合面循環：失效診斷","titleEn":"Impact and mixed-face cycling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「衝擊與混合面循環」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Impact and mixed-face cycling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues. Counting revolutions without interface crossings may wrongly classify localized chipping as a random manufacturing defect rather than repeated loading. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Counting revolutions without interface crossings may wrongly classify localized chipping as a random manufacturing defect rather than repeated loading.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。","textEn":"Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues. Counting revolutions without interface crossings may wrongly classify localized chipping as a random manufacturing defect rather than repeated loading.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「衝擊與混合面循環」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Impact and mixed-face cycling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。","相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues.","The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取樣頻率不足會把衝擊平均掉，刀具卻持續承受疲勞；只統計轉數又忽略硬軟界面轉換，可能誤把局部崩裂當成偶然製造缺陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slow sampling averages impacts away while fatigue continues. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b139-v14-29","title":"刀間距與碴片形成：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cutter spacing and chip formation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「刀間距與碴片形成」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cutter spacing and chip formation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相鄰刀槽之間的裂縫若能連通，岩石以較大碴片剝離；間距、貫入與岩性不匹配時會變成重複研磨。幾何比只描述相對尺度，不能不經試驗就轉成通用最佳刀間距。 假設刀間距80 mm、貫入10 mm，比值s/p=8；相同比值在不同岩性不保證相同比能。 粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「刀間距與碴片形成」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Connected cracks between neighboring tracks release larger chips, while mismatched spacing, penetration and rock behavior promote regrinding. A geometry ratio describes relative scale without establishing a universal optimum spacing absent testing. For assumed spacing 80 mm and penetration 10 mm, s/p=8; the same ratio in different rocks does not guarantee equal specific energy. More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone. Maximizing chip size can also neglect muck-handling capacity and impact limitations in mixed ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cutter spacing and chip formation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「刀間距與碴片形成」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cutter spacing and chip formation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-29-k1","title":"刀間距與碴片形成","titleEn":"Cutter spacing and chip formation","text":"相鄰刀槽之間的裂縫若能連通，岩石以較大碴片剝離；間距、貫入與岩性不匹配時會變成重複研磨。幾何比只描述相對尺度，不能不經試驗就轉成通用最佳刀間距。","textEn":"Connected cracks between neighboring tracks release larger chips, while mismatched spacing, penetration and rock behavior promote regrinding. A geometry ratio describes relative scale without establishing a universal optimum spacing absent testing.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「刀間距與碴片形成」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cutter spacing and chip formation\" is correct?","options":["相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。","只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。","相鄰刀槽之間的裂縫若能連通，岩石以較大碴片剝離；間距、貫入與岩性不匹配時會變成重複研磨。"],"optionsEn":["The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type.","Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing.","Connected cracks between neighboring tracks release larger chips, while mismatched spacing, penetration and rock behavior promote regrinding."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相鄰刀槽之間的裂縫若能連通，岩石以較大碴片剝離；間距、貫入與岩性不匹配時會變成重複研磨。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Connected cracks between neighboring tracks release larger chips, while mismatched spacing, penetration and rock behavior promote regrinding. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b139-v14-30","title":"刀間距與碴片形成：定量估算","titleEn":"Cutter spacing and chip formation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「刀間距與碴片形成」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cutter spacing and chip formation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設刀間距80 mm、貫入10 mm，比值s/p=8；相同比值在不同岩性不保證相同比能。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed spacing 80 mm and penetration 10 mm, s/p=8; the same ratio in different rocks does not guarantee equal specific energy. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照代表岩樣切削試驗、碴片粒徑與實際刀盤配置，記錄岩體節理影響；幾何變更由設計和刀具團隊評估，不能從算例比值直接要求現場改裝刀盤。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare representative cutting tests, chip sizes and actual cutter layout while documenting joints; design and tool teams assess geometry changes, and the example ratio must not directly drive a field cutterhead modification.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設刀間距80 mm、貫入10 mm，比值s/p=8；相同比值在不同岩性不保證相同比能。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed spacing 80 mm and penetration 10 mm, s/p=8; the same ratio in different rocks does not guarantee equal specific energy.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「刀間距與碴片形成」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cutter spacing and chip formation\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。","總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position.","Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b139-v14-31","title":"刀間距與碴片形成：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cutter spacing and chip formation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「刀間距與碴片形成」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cutter spacing and chip formation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照代表岩樣切削試驗、碴片粒徑與實際刀盤配置，記錄岩體節理影響；幾何變更由設計和刀具團隊評估，不能從算例比值直接要求現場改裝刀盤。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare representative cutting tests, chip sizes and actual cutter layout while documenting joints; design and tool teams assess geometry changes, and the example ratio must not directly drive a field cutterhead modification. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone. Maximizing chip size can also neglect muck-handling capacity and impact limitations in mixed ground. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄刀間距與碴片形成的資料來源與適用條件。對照代表岩樣切削試驗、碴片粒徑與實際刀盤配置，記錄岩體節理影響；幾何變更由設計和刀具團隊評估，不能從算例比值直接要求現場改裝刀盤。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for cutter spacing and chip formation. Compare representative cutting tests, chip sizes and actual cutter layout while documenting joints; design and tool teams assess geometry changes, and the example ratio must not directly drive a field cutterhead modification.","failure":"注意干擾：粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照代表岩樣切削試驗、碴片粒徑與實際刀盤配置，記錄岩體節理影響；幾何變更由設計和刀具團隊評估，不能從算例比值直接要求現場改裝刀盤。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。","textEn":"Compare representative cutting tests, chip sizes and actual cutter layout while documenting joints; design and tool teams assess geometry changes, and the example ratio must not directly drive a field cutterhead modification. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone. Maximizing chip size can also neglect muck-handling capacity and impact limitations in mixed ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄刀間距與碴片形成的資料來源與適用條件。對照代表岩樣切削試驗、碴片粒徑與實際刀盤配置，記錄岩體節理影響；幾何變更由設計和刀具團隊評估，不能從算例比值直接要求現場改裝刀盤。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for cutter spacing and chip formation. Compare representative cutting tests, chip sizes and actual cutter layout while documenting joints; design and tool teams assess geometry changes, and the example ratio must not directly drive a field cutterhead modification.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「刀間距與碴片形成」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cutter spacing and chip formation\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","對照代表岩樣切削試驗、碴片粒徑與實際刀盤配置，記錄岩體節理影響；幾何變更由設計和刀具團隊評估，不能從算例比值直接要求現場改裝刀盤。","前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare representative cutting tests, chip sizes and actual cutter layout while documenting joints.","The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照代表岩樣切削試驗、碴片粒徑與實際刀盤配置，記錄岩體節理影響；幾何變更由設計和刀具團隊評估，不能從算例比值直接要求現場改裝刀盤。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare representative cutting tests, chip sizes and actual cutter layout while documenting joints; design and tool teams assess geometry changes, and the example ratio must not directly drive a field cutterhead modification. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b139-v14-32","title":"刀間距與碴片形成：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cutter spacing and chip formation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「刀間距與碴片形成」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cutter spacing and chip formation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone. Maximizing chip size can also neglect muck-handling capacity and impact limitations in mixed ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Maximizing chip size can also neglect muck-handling capacity and impact limitations in mixed ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同刀間距貫入比在所有岩性都會有同樣最佳切削效果。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The same spacing-penetration ratio gives identical optimum cutting in every rock type.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。","textEn":"More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone. Maximizing chip size can also neglect muck-handling capacity and impact limitations in mixed ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「刀間距與碴片形成」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cutter spacing and chip formation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。","粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing.","More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粉碴增加可能表示研磨、磨鈍或岩性改變，不能一律歸於間距不當；若只追求大碴片也可能忽略排碴能力和混合面衝擊的限制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"More fines may indicate regrinding, blunt tools or changed geology rather than spacing alone. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b139-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「刀具身份與維修追溯」與「維護決策與檢查界線」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tool identity and maintenance traceability\" and \"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b139-v14-33","title":"刀具身份與維修追溯：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tool identity and maintenance traceability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「刀具身份與維修追溯」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tool identity and maintenance traceability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同一刀具可能在不同位置使用並經維修，序號、刀位與時間共同決定實際歷程。更換刀環不一定重置軸承壽命，資料庫必須分辨組件層級，否則新舊零件會混成同一壽命樣本。 假設刀環使用400 h更換、軸承此前已200 h，若軸承未換則累積600 h，不是400 h或零。 序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「刀具身份與維修追溯」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A tool may be relocated and rebuilt, making serial number, position and time jointly essential. Replacing a ring does not necessarily reset bearing life; component-level records prevent new and old parts being combined as one lifetime sample. Assume a ring is replaced after 400 h while its bearing already had 200 h; an unchanged bearing has accumulated 600 h, not 400 h or zero. A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life. Supplier comparisons and spare planning then inherit the same erroneous history. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tool identity and maintenance traceability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「刀具身份與維修追溯」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tool identity and maintenance traceability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-33-k1","title":"刀具身份與維修追溯","titleEn":"Tool identity and maintenance traceability","text":"同一刀具可能在不同位置使用並經維修，序號、刀位與時間共同決定實際歷程。更換刀環不一定重置軸承壽命，資料庫必須分辨組件層級，否則新舊零件會混成同一壽命樣本。","textEn":"A tool may be relocated and rebuilt, making serial number, position and time jointly essential. Replacing a ring does not necessarily reset bearing life; component-level records prevent new and old parts being combined as one lifetime sample.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「刀具身份與維修追溯」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tool identity and maintenance traceability\" is correct?","options":["同一刀具可能在不同位置使用並經維修，序號、刀位與時間共同決定實際歷程。","只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。","刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。"],"optionsEn":["A tool may be relocated and rebuilt, making serial number, position and time jointly essential.","Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing.","Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一刀具可能在不同位置使用並經維修，序號、刀位與時間共同決定實際歷程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A tool may be relocated and rebuilt, making serial number, position and time jointly essential. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b139-v14-34","title":"刀具身份與維修追溯：定量估算","titleEn":"Tool identity and maintenance traceability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「刀具身份與維修追溯」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tool identity and maintenance traceability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設刀環使用400 h更換、軸承此前已200 h，若軸承未換則累積600 h，不是400 h或零。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume a ring is replaced after 400 h while its bearing already had 200 h; an unchanged bearing has accumulated 600 h, not 400 h or zero. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查刀位圖與序號、維修單、照片和量測紀錄能否互相連接，重建組件累積里程；資料負責人與維修主管共同確認重置規則，缺失歷程需標示不確定而非補寫理想值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit links among cutter map, serials, maintenance sheets, photographs and measurements and reconstruct component exposure; data and maintenance leads approve reset rules, flagging missing history instead of filling it with idealized values.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設刀環使用400 h更換、軸承此前已200 h，若軸承未換則累積600 h，不是400 h或零。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume a ring is replaced after 400 h while its bearing already had 200 h; an unchanged bearing has accumulated 600 h, not 400 h or zero.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「刀具身份與維修追溯」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tool identity and maintenance traceability\", which statement holds?","options":["每轉進尺越大就必定代表切削效率和刀具壽命越好。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","旋轉比能增加只能由岩石變硬造成，與排碴無關。"],"optionsEn":["Greater penetration per revolution necessarily improves cutting efficiency and cutter life.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Higher rotational specific energy can only come from harder rock, never muck removal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b139-v14-35","title":"刀具身份與維修追溯：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tool identity and maintenance traceability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「刀具身份與維修追溯」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tool identity and maintenance traceability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查刀位圖與序號、維修單、照片和量測紀錄能否互相連接，重建組件累積里程；資料負責人與維修主管共同確認重置規則，缺失歷程需標示不確定而非補寫理想值。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit links among cutter map, serials, maintenance sheets, photographs and measurements and reconstruct component exposure; data and maintenance leads approve reset rules, flagging missing history instead of filling it with idealized values. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life. Supplier comparisons and spare planning then inherit the same erroneous history. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄刀具身份與維修追溯的資料來源與適用條件。抽查刀位圖與序號、維修單、照片和量測紀錄能否互相連接，重建組件累積里程；資料負責人與維修主管共同確認重置規則，缺失歷程需標示不確定而非補寫理想值。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for tool identity and maintenance traceability. Audit links among cutter map, serials, maintenance sheets, photographs and measurements and reconstruct component exposure; data and maintenance leads approve reset rules, flagging missing history instead of filling it with idealized values.","failure":"注意干擾：序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查刀位圖與序號、維修單、照片和量測紀錄能否互相連接，重建組件累積里程；資料負責人與維修主管共同確認重置規則，缺失歷程需標示不確定而非補寫理想值。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。","textEn":"Audit links among cutter map, serials, maintenance sheets, photographs and measurements and reconstruct component exposure; data and maintenance leads approve reset rules, flagging missing history instead of filling it with idealized values. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life. Supplier comparisons and spare planning then inherit the same erroneous history.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄刀具身份與維修追溯的資料來源與適用條件。抽查刀位圖與序號、維修單、照片和量測紀錄能否互相連接，重建組件累積里程；資料負責人與維修主管共同確認重置規則，缺失歷程需標示不確定而非補寫理想值。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for tool identity and maintenance traceability. Audit links among cutter map, serials, maintenance sheets, photographs and measurements and reconstruct component exposure; data and maintenance leads approve reset rules, flagging missing history instead of filling it with idealized values.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「刀具身份與維修追溯」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tool identity and maintenance traceability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","刀環剩餘直徑足夠就證明軸承和轉動狀態也正常。","抽查刀位圖與序號、維修單、照片和量測紀錄能否互相連接，重建組件累積里程；資料負責人與維修主管共同確認重置規則，缺失歷程需標示不確定而非補寫理想值。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adequate remaining ring diameter proves that bearings and rotation are also healthy.","Audit links among cutter map, serials, maintenance sheets, photographs and measurements and reconstruct component exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"抽查刀位圖與序號、維修單、照片和量測紀錄能否互相連接，重建組件累積里程；資料負責人與維修主管共同確認重置規則，缺失歷程需標示不確定而非補寫理想值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit links among cutter map, serials, maintenance sheets, photographs and measurements and reconstruct component exposure; data and maintenance leads approve reset rules, flagging missing history instead of filling it with idealized values. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b139-v14-36","title":"刀具身份與維修追溯：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tool identity and maintenance traceability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「刀具身份與維修追溯」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tool identity and maintenance traceability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life. Supplier comparisons and spare planning then inherit the same erroneous history. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Supplier comparisons and spare planning then inherit the same erroneous history.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只更換刀環就可以把未更換軸承的累積使用時間歸零。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Replacing only the ring resets accumulated service time of the unchanged bearing.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。","textEn":"A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life. Supplier comparisons and spare planning then inherit the same erroneous history.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「刀具身份與維修追溯」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tool identity and maintenance traceability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。"],"optionsEn":["A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"序號抄錯會把早期故障歸到另一批次，更換整刀與只換刀環未區分則誇大或低估壽命；供應比較和備件計畫都會被錯誤歷程影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A wrong serial assigns early failure to the wrong batch, while conflating complete-tool and ring-only replacement distorts life. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b139-v14-37","title":"維護決策與檢查界線：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「維護決策與檢查界線」如何影響潛盾機刀具磨耗管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Maintenance decisions and access boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “TBM cutter-wear management”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"刀具維護需整合剩餘厚度、軸承狀態、預測地層與可檢查窗口，不能由單一磨耗率自動決定。資料驅動判讀只支持專業決策，刀盤或加壓艙的接近仍是獨立的高風險核准工作。 假設40刀中36刀有最新有效狀態，覆蓋90%；其餘4刀若位於同一高負荷區，不能以整體比例忽略。 只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「維護決策與檢查界線」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Maintenance combines remaining section, bearing condition, predicted ground and inspection opportunities rather than one wear rate. Data supports professional decisions, while access to a cutterhead or pressurized chamber remains a separately approved specialist task. If 36 of an assumed 40 cutters have current valid condition records, coverage is 90%; 4 missing tools in a high-load zone cannot be dismissed by the overall percentage. Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts. Ignoring these limits can turn planning numbers into mistakenly assumed authorization for field work. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Maintenance decisions and access boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「維護決策與檢查界線」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Maintenance decisions and access boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-37-k1","title":"維護決策與檢查界線","titleEn":"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries","text":"刀具維護需整合剩餘厚度、軸承狀態、預測地層與可檢查窗口，不能由單一磨耗率自動決定。資料驅動判讀只支持專業決策，刀盤或加壓艙的接近仍是獨立的高風險核准工作。","textEn":"Maintenance combines remaining section, bearing condition, predicted ground and inspection opportunities rather than one wear rate. Data supports professional decisions, while access to a cutterhead or pressurized chamber remains a separately approved specialist task.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「維護決策與檢查界線」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries\" is correct?","options":["刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。","刀具維護需整合剩餘厚度、軸承狀態、預測地層與可檢查窗口，不能由單一磨耗率自動決定。","所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter.","Maintenance combines remaining section, bearing condition, predicted ground and inspection opportunities rather than one wear rate.","Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"刀具維護需整合剩餘厚度、軸承狀態、預測地層與可檢查窗口，不能由單一磨耗率自動決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Maintenance combines remaining section, bearing condition, predicted ground and inspection opportunities rather than one wear rate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b139-v14-38","title":"維護決策與檢查界線：定量估算","titleEn":"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「維護決策與檢查界線」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Maintenance decisions and access boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設40刀中36刀有最新有效狀態，覆蓋90%；其餘4刀若位於同一高負荷區，不能以整體比例忽略。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If 36 of an assumed 40 cutters have current valid condition records, coverage is 90%; 4 missing tools in a high-load zone cannot be dismissed by the overall percentage. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以刀位風險圖核對資料新鮮度、地質預測和維護紀錄，將未確認刀具單列；維修及施工負責人依核准計畫安排檢查，課程不提供進艙、換刀或解除隔離的操作步驟。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Review data freshness, ground prediction and maintenance on a position-risk map, listing unconfirmed tools; maintenance and construction leads plan inspections under approved arrangements, with no chamber-entry or tool-change procedure supplied here.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設40刀中36刀有最新有效狀態，覆蓋90%；其餘4刀若位於同一高負荷區，不能以整體比例忽略。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If 36 of an assumed 40 cutters have current valid condition records, coverage is 90%; 4 missing tools in a high-load zone cannot be dismissed by the overall percentage.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「維護決策與檢查界線」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["總推力除刀具數就能得到每顆刀實際承受的峰值荷重。","前一岩層的平均磨耗率可以無條件預測下一岩層壽命。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Total thrust divided by cutter count gives each cutter's actual peak load.","The previous stratum's mean wear rate predicts life in the next stratum unconditionally.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b139-v14-39","title":"維護決策與檢查界線：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「維護決策與檢查界線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Maintenance decisions and access boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以刀位風險圖核對資料新鮮度、地質預測和維護紀錄，將未確認刀具單列；維修及施工負責人依核准計畫安排檢查，課程不提供進艙、換刀或解除隔離的操作步驟。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Review data freshness, ground prediction and maintenance on a position-risk map, listing unconfirmed tools; maintenance and construction leads plan inspections under approved arrangements, with no chamber-entry or tool-change procedure supplied here. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts. Ignoring these limits can turn planning numbers into mistakenly assumed authorization for field work. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄維護決策與檢查界線的資料來源與適用條件。以刀位風險圖核對資料新鮮度、地質預測和維護紀錄，將未確認刀具單列；維修及施工負責人依核准計畫安排檢查，課程不提供進艙、換刀或解除隔離的操作步驟。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for maintenance decisions and access boundaries. Review data freshness, ground prediction and maintenance on a position-risk map, listing unconfirmed tools; maintenance and construction leads plan inspections under approved arrangements, with no chamber-entry or tool-change procedure supplied here.","failure":"注意干擾：只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以刀位風險圖核對資料新鮮度、地質預測和維護紀錄，將未確認刀具單列；維修及施工負責人依核准計畫安排檢查，課程不提供進艙、換刀或解除隔離的操作步驟。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。","textEn":"Review data freshness, ground prediction and maintenance on a position-risk map, listing unconfirmed tools; maintenance and construction leads plan inspections under approved arrangements, with no chamber-entry or tool-change procedure supplied here. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts. Ignoring these limits can turn planning numbers into mistakenly assumed authorization for field work.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄維護決策與檢查界線的資料來源與適用條件。以刀位風險圖核對資料新鮮度、地質預測和維護紀錄，將未確認刀具單列；維修及施工負責人依核准計畫安排檢查，課程不提供進艙、換刀或解除隔離的操作步驟。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for maintenance decisions and access boundaries. Review data freshness, ground prediction and maintenance on a position-risk map, listing unconfirmed tools; maintenance and construction leads plan inspections under approved arrangements, with no chamber-entry or tool-change procedure supplied here.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「維護決策與檢查界線」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries\"?","options":["以刀位風險圖核對資料新鮮度、地質預測和維護紀錄，將未確認刀具單列；維修及施工負責人依核准計畫安排檢查，課程不提供進艙、換刀或解除隔離的操作步驟。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","班平均扭矩正常就表示沒有局部刀具衝擊疲勞。"],"optionsEn":["Review data freshness, ground prediction and maintenance on a position-risk map, listing unconfirmed tools.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Normal shift-average torque means no localized cutter impact fatigue is occurring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以刀位風險圖核對資料新鮮度、地質預測和維護紀錄，將未確認刀具單列；維修及施工負責人依核准計畫安排檢查，課程不提供進艙、換刀或解除隔離的操作步驟。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Review data freshness, ground prediction and maintenance on a position-risk map, listing unconfirmed tools; maintenance and construction leads plan inspections under approved arrangements, with no chamber-entry or tool-change procedure supplied here. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b139-v14-40","title":"維護決策與檢查界線：失效診斷","titleEn":"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b139-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「維護決策與檢查界線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Maintenance decisions and access boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts. Ignoring these limits can turn planning numbers into mistakenly assumed authorization for field work. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ignoring these limits can turn planning numbers into mistakenly assumed authorization for field work.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀具平均磨耗很低就能排除任何單刀卡死風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low average cutter wear excludes any possibility of one seized cutter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b139-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。","textEn":"Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts. Ignoring these limits can turn planning numbers into mistakenly assumed authorization for field work.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b139-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「維護決策與檢查界線」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Maintenance decisions and access boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。","所有刀位轉數相同時，接觸行程和磨耗需求也完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts.","Equal revolutions give identical contact travel and wear demand at every cutter position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只按平均磨耗安排檢查可能漏掉一顆卡死刀具，預測模型若未更新新岩層也會過度樂觀；忽略這些限制會讓規劃數字被誤當現場許可。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Average-wear scheduling can miss one seized tool, and an unupdated ground model gives optimistic forecasts. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-tools","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
